WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.283 --> 00:00:01.116
(soft instrumental music)

00:00:01.116 --> 00:00:04.188
- As far as my eyes go, I feel like people

00:00:04.188 --> 00:00:05.301
don't really pay them any mind.

00:00:05.301 --> 00:00:09.192
- I've never gotten any
compliments on my eyes.

00:00:09.192 --> 00:00:11.296
- I always feel invisible
with my blue eyes.

00:00:11.296 --> 00:00:13.499
I feel really clear looking.

00:00:13.499 --> 00:00:16.934
(logo whooshes)
(hinge squeaks)

00:00:16.934 --> 00:00:19.138
- I've totally wanted to try blue eyes.

00:00:19.138 --> 00:00:20.839
Playing with color is always cool.

00:00:20.839 --> 00:00:22.811
- Growing up in the South,
like having light skin,

00:00:22.811 --> 00:00:24.473
light eyes is very celebrated

00:00:24.473 --> 00:00:27.163
so growing up, I always
wanted to have light eyes.

00:00:27.163 --> 00:00:31.155
- I'm the only one in my
family that has blue eyes.

00:00:31.155 --> 00:00:32.531
I have six siblings.

00:00:32.531 --> 00:00:35.375
I always wanted brown eyes
just 'cause everybody else

00:00:35.375 --> 00:00:36.732
in my family has them.

00:00:36.732 --> 00:00:38.380
- Today what we're going to do is change

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:41.272
the eye color of three different patients.

00:00:41.272 --> 00:00:43.752
Now the fitting of contact
lenses, whether they be

00:00:43.752 --> 00:00:45.591
just purely for cosmetic purposes

00:00:45.591 --> 00:00:47.203
or for the correction of vision,

00:00:47.203 --> 00:00:49.938
it's still a medical device
and one needs to be examined

00:00:49.938 --> 00:00:52.955
by an eye doctor to be fit appropriately.

00:00:52.955 --> 00:00:54.597
- I'm going to be trying blue eyes.

00:00:54.597 --> 00:00:56.066
- I'm going to be trying out green eyes.

00:00:56.066 --> 00:00:58.255
- And I'm going to be trying brown eyes.

00:00:58.255 --> 00:01:00.765
- So Kane, we've got both lenses in now.

00:01:00.765 --> 00:01:04.343
(Kane sighs heavily)
Check it out.

00:01:04.343 --> 00:01:06.017
- [Kane] Whoa!

00:01:06.017 --> 00:01:07.100
- Oh my geez!

00:01:07.998 --> 00:01:09.649
- [Kuwilileni] Whoa!

00:01:09.649 --> 00:01:12.225
- It feels like I put
someone's eyeball into my head.

00:01:12.225 --> 00:01:13.387
- Who am I?

00:01:13.387 --> 00:01:16.329
- I expected to hate this,
but actually kind of love it.

00:01:16.329 --> 00:01:18.344
- I feel like the reaction
is going to be positive

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:20.649
because it's such a cool thing to change.

00:01:20.649 --> 00:01:23.256
- I am a little bit nervous
about wearing colored contacts

00:01:23.256 --> 00:01:25.219
'cause I'm worried that people will think

00:01:25.219 --> 00:01:27.556
that I don't think that my own brown eyes,

00:01:27.556 --> 00:01:29.689
as they are, are beautiful enough.

00:01:29.689 --> 00:01:32.359
- I assume people will
notice that something

00:01:32.359 --> 00:01:34.028
on my face is darker.

00:01:34.028 --> 00:01:37.202
The guy who helped me put
the lenses in was like,

00:01:37.202 --> 00:01:39.774
"You look like a completely
different person."

00:01:39.774 --> 00:01:41.732
I do look like the rest of my family.

00:01:41.732 --> 00:01:44.217
- I feel just like augmenting
one part of my body

00:01:44.217 --> 00:01:46.270
has made me feel like more beautiful.

00:01:46.270 --> 00:01:48.445
I think I'm going to become really vain,

00:01:48.445 --> 00:01:50.608
like even now I'm like, "Hey, girl."

00:01:50.608 --> 00:01:53.472
- I look less like a cyborg
today and more like a cat.

00:01:53.472 --> 00:01:55.461
- So I just put 'em in
for the second time.

00:01:55.461 --> 00:01:56.732
I feel like I've acclimated to them

00:01:56.732 --> 00:01:59.797
and they just look like my
normal eyes but they kinda hurt.

00:01:59.797 --> 00:02:02.869
I don't understand how
people do this every morning.

00:02:02.869 --> 00:02:04.814
- I feel like a lot bolder.

00:02:04.814 --> 00:02:06.911
I like being another person.

00:02:06.911 --> 00:02:08.976
I feel like people look at me different.

00:02:08.976 --> 00:02:11.318
- Whoa, you look like a demon.
(whimsical instrumental music)

00:02:11.318 --> 00:02:13.209
- I don't know what my
boyfriend will feel,

00:02:13.209 --> 00:02:15.273
like will he dump me?

00:02:15.273 --> 00:02:17.263
I don't know, we'll see.

00:02:17.263 --> 00:02:18.096
- Whoa.

00:02:19.725 --> 00:02:23.073
I'm very used to you with the blue eyes.

00:02:23.073 --> 00:02:24.941
I don't know, they're like piercing.

00:02:24.941 --> 00:02:28.467
- Say some people some
time to get used to it but,

00:02:28.467 --> 00:02:30.005
yeah, I totally dig it.

00:02:30.005 --> 00:02:31.833
- You look like a mutant from X-Men.

00:02:31.833 --> 00:02:34.937
- They're entrancing, I'm entranced.

00:02:34.937 --> 00:02:36.824
- I think it's going to
be weird for my boyfriend.

00:02:36.824 --> 00:02:37.659
- Is this a trick?

00:02:37.659 --> 00:02:39.658
- [Kane] Do you notice
something different?

00:02:39.658 --> 00:02:40.491
My eyes?

00:02:41.611 --> 00:02:43.010
- Uh-huh, yeah, your eyes are different.

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:45.742
Ah, nu-uh! (laughs)

00:02:45.742 --> 00:02:46.575
Are they blue?

00:02:46.575 --> 00:02:47.408
- [Kane] Yeah.
(laughs)

00:02:47.408 --> 00:02:48.498
- Oh my gosh!

00:02:48.498 --> 00:02:50.224
- One of the things I've
noticed about wearing them

00:02:50.224 --> 00:02:52.174
is I'm always wondering if
people are going to notice.

00:02:52.174 --> 00:02:53.568
- They kind of fit.

00:02:53.568 --> 00:02:56.457
- They're like brighter, it
like hits you in the face.

00:02:56.457 --> 00:02:57.540
- Ah, gotcha!

00:02:58.802 --> 00:03:00.385
Going in the trash!

00:03:01.358 --> 00:03:03.191
Bye, no more contacts.

00:03:04.428 --> 00:03:06.034
I enjoyed the experience a lot,

00:03:06.034 --> 00:03:07.708
of just seeing what I would look like

00:03:07.708 --> 00:03:10.401
but it was a lot of torture to get there.

00:03:10.401 --> 00:03:11.709
- I was shocked when I put them in

00:03:11.709 --> 00:03:13.029
that I actually liked them.

00:03:13.029 --> 00:03:16.126
I was apprehensive because
having come into myself

00:03:16.126 --> 00:03:18.225
and really celebrating and loving myself,

00:03:18.225 --> 00:03:20.857
I was afraid society would
think that I was trying

00:03:20.857 --> 00:03:23.334
to hide my African heritage.

00:03:23.334 --> 00:03:26.135
- It totally made my dreams come true.

00:03:26.135 --> 00:03:28.520
Do I look like a part of my family now?

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:31.201
I think they're like, "Finally."

00:03:31.201 --> 00:03:33.224
- One of the most powerful
lessons I've learned in life

00:03:33.224 --> 00:03:36.962
is living your body as it is,
as it changes, as it grows,

00:03:36.962 --> 00:03:38.677
like loving it for what it is.

00:03:38.677 --> 00:03:41.603
- And once I died, the
mortician will be like,

00:03:41.603 --> 00:03:44.536
"Oh, this is weird," like,

00:03:44.536 --> 00:03:45.487
(hacks)

00:03:45.487 --> 00:03:48.249
"This 90-year-old woman has
contacts in." (chuckles)

